4.x group)\n3. srd006-cat remaining requirements (R5.x group)  \n4. srd011-magefiles/cmd/version\n\nLet me verify weight budgets. Without the actual weights file, I'll keep each task to 4 sub-requirements and assume weight=1 (the default). If any requirement has weight > 1, the 4-requirement limit provides buffer.\n\nActually, I need to be more careful. The constraints say \"Each task's total requirement weight must not exceed 4\" and I must \"list the requirements you plan to include and their weights from requirements.yaml.\" Since I cannot read requirements.yaml (no tool calls allowed), I must work with what's provided.\n\nThe constraint also says each task contains \"at most 4 SRD sub-requirements.\" With default weight=1, 4 requirements = weight 4 = the maximum. So I'll stick to exactly 4 sub-requirements per task.\n\nFor srd086-hashutil (9 ready requirements), I need 3 tasks minimum. But I only have 4 task slots total.\n\nLet me reconsider priorities. The contracts exist in package_contracts for hashutil. hashutil serves the checksum utilities in releases 05.4 and 09.0, which are far out. Meanwhile, srd006-cat (release 01.1) has 13 remaining requirements and is closer to completion.\n\nBut per P1 (release-driven priority), release 00.0 is earliest incomplete. hashutil is in 00.0. So hashutil takes priority over cat.\n\nHowever, srd011-magefiles is also 00.0. cmd/version is simpler.\n\nPlan:\n1. srd086-hashutil contract task (since it's a new package) — but wait, the contract is already defined in package_contracts. The constraint says \"propose a contract task that defines all exported types, interfaces, and function signatures as Go stubs\" for NEW packages. hashutil doesn't exist yet.\n2. srd086-hashutil implementation part 1\n3. srd086-hashutil implementation part 2  \n4. srd011-magefiles/cmd/version\n\nActually, the contract task counts toward the 4-task limit. Let me fit this:\n\n1. srd086-hashutil contract (R1.1-R1.4 — types and signatures)\n2. srd086-hashutil implementation (R2.1-R2.3, R3.1 — core functions)\n3. srd086-hashutil implementation (R3.2 + srd011 R1.1 — verify + version... no, these are different packages)\n4. srd011-magefiles cmd/version (R1.1, R2.1, R3.1, R4.1)\n\nWait, but srd011 has 5 ready requirements: R1.1, R2.1, R3.1, R4.1, R5.1. That's 5, exceeds 4. I'd need to split or combine sensibly.\n\nLet me finalize:\n\n```\nTask 0: srd086-hashutil contract (defines types/signatures as stubs)\n  Requirements: R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4 (4 reqs, weight ≤ 4)\n\nTask 1: srd086-hashutil implementation — formatting and digest (depends on task 0)\n  Requirements: R2.1, R2.2, R2.3 (3 reqs, weight ≤ 4) \n\nTask 2: srd086-hashutil implementation — verify and digest files (depends on task 1)\n  Requirements: R3.1, R3.2 (2 reqs, weight ≤ 4)\n\nTask 3: srd011-magefiles cmd/version (R1.1, R2.1, R3.1, R4.1) \n  4 reqs, weight ≤ 4. R5.1 goes to next batch.\n```\n\nBut wait — I need to check: does cmd/version already exist? The source_code section isn't provided explicitly, but the analysis shows codestatus \"not started\" for rel00.0-uc001-magefiles. And srd011 R5.1 is \"ready\". cmd/version is a separate directory from magefiles.\n\nAlso — the contract task for hashutil should include the dependency=-1 per constraints. And srd011/cmd/version — does it need a contract? It's a simple cmd/ binary, not a pkg/. The contract requirement applies to new packages (libraries), not cmd/ binaries.\n\nLet me also reconsider: does srd011 cmd/version need testutils? Looking at the shared_protocols — every cmd/ package uses differential testing. But testutils isn't in requirement_states (no \"ready\" items), so I can't propose testutils implementation. cmd/version's test would need testutils... but the SRD for version (srd059) only shows R1.5 as ready. And srd011-magefiles includes the version binary.\n\nThis is getting complex. Let me simplify and focus on what I can definitively propose:\n\n**hashutil** (3 tasks) + **cmd/version** (1 task) = 4 tasks.\n\nFor cmd/version, the test file would use testutils, but since version is simple (prints version string), the test might be standalone. The srd059-version R1.5 is ready. srd011-magefiles R1.1-R5.1 are ready. I'll combine srd011 + srd059 requirements for the version binary since they overlap.\n\nLet me finalize the output.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/hashutil types and contracts (srd086-hashutil R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd086-hashutil.yaml (full SRD for hashutil package)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/ component structure and import constraints)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (reference for pkg/ package structure conventions)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"HashConfig, CheckOptions types; FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ComputeDigest, ParseChecksumLine, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles function signatures as stubs\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Define HashConfig struct with fields: Algorithm string, NewHash func() hash.Hash, DigestLen int per srd086-hashutil R1.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Define CheckOptions struct with fields: Warn bool, Quiet bool, Status bool per srd086-hashutil R1.2\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Define FormatGNU(digest, filename string, binary bool) string and FormatBSDTag(algorithm, filename, digest string) string function signatures returning placeholder values per srd086-hashutil R1.3\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Define ComputeDigest, ParseChecksumLine, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles function signatures returning placeholder values per srd086-hashutil R1.4\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Package path is pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go. The package name is hashutil.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"All exported function signatures match the contract exactly: FormatGNU(digest, filename string, binary bool) string; FormatBSDTag(algorithm, filename, digest string) string; ComputeDigest(r io.Reader, cfg HashConfig) (string, error); ParseChecksumLine(line string, cfg HashConfig) (filename, expectedDigest string, binary bool, err error); VerifyChecksums(checksumFile string, cfg HashConfig, opts CheckOptions, stdout, stderr io.Writer) (bool, error); DigestFiles(files []string, cfg HashConfig, binary, tag bool, stdout, stderr io.Writer) int\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Imports allowed: hash, io, os, fmt, encoding/hex, bufio, strings, regexp. Must not import any cmd/ package or any other pkg/ package.\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Stub functions should return zero values. This is a contract task -- full implementation follows in subsequent tasks.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go exists and compiles with go vet ./pkg/hashutil/...\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"HashConfig and CheckOptions structs are exported with all specified fields\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"All six exported functions have correct signatures matching the contract\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"No imports from cmd/ or other pkg/ packages\"\n\n- index: 1\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/hashutil formatting and digest computation (srd086-hashutil R2.1, R2.2, R2.3)\"\n  dependency: 0\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd086-hashutil.yaml (full SRD for hashutil package)\n      - pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go (contract types and function signatures from task 0)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Implement FormatGNU, FormatBSDTag, ComputeDigest, ParseChecksumLine\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement FormatGNU to produce GNU two-space format: for text mode output 'DIGEST  FILENAME', for binary mode output 'DIGEST *FILENAME' per srd086-hashutil R2.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement FormatBSDTag to produce BSD tag format: 'ALGORITHM (FILENAME) = DIGEST' per srd086-hashutil R2.2\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement ComputeDigest to read all bytes from r, hash them using cfg.NewHash(), and return the hex-encoded digest string per srd086-hashutil R2.3\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"ComputeDigest reads the io.Reader in chunks using io.Copy into the hash, then hex-encodes the Sum result\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"FormatGNU uses two spaces between digest and filename for text mode, asterisk prefix on filename for binary mode\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"FormatGNU returns 'digest  filename' for text mode and 'digest *filename' for binary mode\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"FormatBSDTag returns 'ALGORITHM (filename) = digest'\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"ComputeDigest returns correct hex digest for any hash function provided via HashConfig.NewHash\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/hashutil/... passes with no errors\"\n\n- index: 2\n  title: \"[stitch] pkg/hashutil checksum parsing, verification, and file digesting (srd086-hashutil R3.1, R3.2)\"\n  dependency: 1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd086-hashutil.yaml (full SRD for hashutil package)\n      - pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go (types and formatting functions from tasks 0-1)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/hashutil/hashutil.go\n        action: modify\n        note: \"Implement ParseChecksumLine, VerifyChecksums, DigestFiles\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement ParseChecksumLine to parse both GNU format ('DIGEST  FILENAME' and 'DIGEST *FILENAME') and BSD tag format ('ALGORITHM (FILENAME) = DIGEST') lines, returning filename, expected digest, binary flag, and error per srd086-hashutil R3.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement VerifyChecksums to read a checksum file line by line, parse each line with ParseChecksumLine, compute the digest of each referenced file, compare against the expected digest, and report results (OK/FAILED) to stdout/stderr respecting CheckOptions (Warn, Quiet, Status flags). Implement DigestFiles to compute and print digests for a list of files using FormatGNU or FormatBSDTag based on the tag flag, reading from stdin when files list contains '-' per srd086-hashutil R3.2\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"ParseChecksumLine uses regexp to detect GNU vs BSD tag format and extract fields accordingly\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"VerifyChecksums returns (allOK bool, err error) where allOK is false if any file failed verification\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"DigestFiles returns an int exit code: 0 if all files digested successfully, 1 if any file could not be read\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"When files list contains '-', read from os.Stdin and use '-' as the filename in output\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"ParseChecksumLine correctly parses GNU text, GNU binary, and BSD tag format lines\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"VerifyChecksums reads checksum file, computes digests, compares, and prints OK/FAILED per line\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"DigestFiles computes and prints digests for each file in the list, supporting stdin via '-'\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/hashutil/... passes with no errors\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"CheckOptions.Quiet suppresses OK lines, Warn prints warnings for malformed lines, Status suppresses all output and uses exit code only\"\n\n- index: 3\n  title: \"[stitch] cmd/version binary (srd011-magefiles R1.1, R2.1, R3.1, R4.1)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd011-magefiles.yaml (SRD for magefiles and cmd/version)\n      - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd059-version.yaml (SRD for version command)\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (cmd/ component structure and SIGPIPE protocol)\n      - pkg/sys/sys.go (InstallSIGPIPEHandler function for SIGPIPE handling)\n\n    files:\n      - path: cmd/version/main.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Version binary that prints version information\"\n      - path: cmd/version/version_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: \"Tests for version binary\"\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Create cmd/version/main.go that prints the project version string to stdout and exits 0 per srd011-magefiles R1.1\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per srd011-magefiles R2.1\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Version string is set via Go linker flags (-ldflags -X) with a default fallback value of 'dev' when not set per srd011-magefiles R3.1\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Print version string followed by a newline to stdout per srd011-magefiles R4.1\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use a package-level var version = 'dev' that is overwritten by -ldflags '-X main.version=VALUE' at build time\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Output format is the version string followed by a newline, nothing else\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Test builds the binary with testutils.BuildBinary and verifies the output contains 'dev' when no ldflags are set. If testutils is not available, test directly with go build and exec.Command.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"cmd/version/main.go compiles with go build -o bin/version ./cmd/version/\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"Running bin/version prints 'dev' followed by a newline when built without ldflags\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() is called at the start of main\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"go test ./cmd/version/... -count=1 passes\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_